<metadata_system id="002" name="Windows NTFS File Data" category="OS" category_label="Operating System / File System" used_for="Windows filesystem metadata (MFT-resident attributes)" spec_source="Microsoft NTFS specification; Brian Carrier 'File System Forensic Analysis' Ch. 12-13" completeness="comprehensive" record_count="47">
  <description>NTFS stores all file metadata as numbered attributes within Master File Table (MFT) records. Each attribute has a type code (e.g. 0x10 = $STANDARD_INFORMATION) and may be resident (small, in MFT record) or non-resident (large, with extents pointing to clusters). This list covers all major attribute types defined in the NTFS specification.</description>
